And of course the fun part, the roleplay!

Since I'm atheist, I'd like to know what, exactly, can I do that won't
break the conduct.  For example, kicking an altar, or sitting on it,
or engraving on it - will those break the conduct?

If I do something to the altar in a temple (aside from sacrifice on a
cross-aligned one), will it also piss off the priest?  I know jumping
and bumping into a priest will anger the priest (I did it before).

Anyway here are some reflections on Nethack atheism:
1.  You have to keep track of resistances, really.  I tended to lose
track of them, because somewhere along the way I would pray so much
that I'd be crowned, which gives all the important resistances.  For
example, I thought I could still bop Medusa even though she had a wand
of lightning - but I forgot that I didn't have shock resistance.
2.  You really, really have to avoid bad situations.  I thought I was
able to do that, but it turns out I'm a little too reliant on my god's
get-out-of-bad-situation-free card.  Going atheist forced me to stand
behind my pet, even at early stages, so that he would be powerful
enough to have a go at the Minetown watchmen and I could pick through
their armor.
3.  Priest's HP growth sucks, so standing behind pets is really a good
idea regardless of theism or lack thereof.



